  "notes": [
    "How it works: you play Elden Ring as V1 from ULTRAKILL. A real ULTRAKILL runs hidden and gives you its movement and weapons (dashes, slides, whiplash, coins, rockets, parries, style meter) against Elden Ring's enemies and bosses, offline.",
    "The Play button does not start it: run launch-eldenkill.bat in %LOCALAPPDATA%\\SIGF\\profiles\\sigf-eldenkill\\eldenring, not as admin. Elden Ring starts offline (Easy Anti-Cheat off) and starts ULTRAKILL by itself, hidden. Load a character: once the floor has loaded, V1 takes over.",
    "Keys: ULTRAKILL's own (WASD, Space, Shift dash, Ctrl slide, mouse aim and shoot, 1-5 weapons, F punch, R whiplash), plus E to interact (doors, graces, items, NPCs), Esc Elden Ring's menu, F1 ULTRAKILL's options, F9 V1 off/on, F7 unstick V1.",
    "You need Elden Ring (exe 2.7.1.0) and ULTRAKILL, both on Steam, Windows only, and me3 0.13.0 installed with its me3_installer.exe. If ULTRAKILL is not in the default Steam folder, D:\\SteamLibrary or Desktop\\ULTRAKILL, set \"ultrakill = <path>\\ULTRAKILL.exe\" in eldenkill.ini in the profile folder.",
    "Offline only, never online: Elden Ring's anti-tamper is turned off too. Its own save EldenKill.sl2 keeps your normal save untouched (copy ER0000.sl2 to EldenKill.sl2 in %APPDATA%\\EldenRing\\<id> to bring a character); Restore leaves it. 16 GB of RAM stutters: two games run at once.",
    "Work in progress: you may fall through the map, hit invisible walls or get stuck; enemies do not flinch and big bosses hit very hard. The release zip is not tied to an exact commit (SIGF scanned and reviewed it). Report bugs to the author with eldenkill.log; F6 saves a snapshot of your spot."
  ]
